Short : Zany Golf Enhanced 2.0b: HD-Installer with smooth frames
Type : game/patch
Author : Vesuri, after Bored Seal (v1.0, v1.1)

This patch applies to "Zany Golf" by Electronic Arts (c) 1988.
Slave requires WHDLOAD V17+.
Game requires 0.5MB ChipRAM (+ 0.7MB RAM for PreLoad,
+ 88KB for faster drawing, best Fast memory)

FEATURES:
- Full load from HD
- Disk protection removed
- Trainer key added (pressing F10 will give you 9 strokes)
- OS emulation module used
- ROM/NI icon (created by JHZ)
- Quit option (your default key)

HISTORY:
version 2.0b (17.11.2026) done by Vesuri:
- smooth movement at the game's intended speed on every Amiga: frames are
  drawn between the game's steps, up to one per display frame on a 68030,
  and drawn faster on every Amiga, the A500 included
- the mouse pointer moves every display frame, fast strokes stay straight
  and clicks are no longer missed
- Esc or the mouse button skips the opening credits
- no pause after pressing 1-4 at the title
- the bonus, award and game over screens and the fades last as long on
  every Amiga as on an A500
- uses fast memory and the instruction cache when available
- "Start on hole" option in the WHDLoad splash window

v1.0 (05-Aug-2000) - first release
V1.1 (23-Jul-2006) - disk access removed, files moved to "data" subdirectory


Thanks to Jan Vieten for disk image.

